  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): ガジュツ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AC%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A5%E3%83%84",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 108911524,
      "text": "ガジュツ は、ショウガ科ウコン属の1種の多年草。別名紫ウコン・夏ウコンともいうが、ウコン 、春ウコン とは別種である。沖縄ではムラサキウッチン、屋久島ではガゼツともいう。英語名はゼドアリー（zedoary）、またはホワイトターメリック。タイ名はマハーメーク。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Curcuma zedoaria",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curcuma_zedoaria",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1340334620,
      "text": "Curcuma zedoaria is a perennial herb and member of the genus Curcuma, family Zingiberaceae. The plant is native to South Asia and Southeast Asia but is now naturalized in other places including the US state of Florida. Zedoary was one of the ancient food plants of the Austronesian peoples. They were spread during prehistoric times to the Pacific Islands and Madagascar during the Austronesian expansion. Its use as a spice in the West today is extremely rare, having been replaced by ginger, and to a lesser extent, yellow turmeric."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Curcuma zedoaria",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curcuma_zedoaria",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 163729174,
      "text": "El tamoilán de Filipinas o cedoaria es una especie de planta herbácea perteneciente a la familia de las zingiberáceas. Es originaria del sur y sudeste de Asia."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Zédoaire",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z%C3%A9doaire",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 224828590,
      "text": "La zédoaire est une espèce de plantes à fleurs du genre Curcuma et de la famille des Zingibéracées. C'est une plante herbacée rhizomateuse vivace originaire de l'Inde et de l'Indonésie."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Curcuma zedoaria",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curcuma_zedoaria",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 71358421,
      "text": "Curcuma zedoaria é uma espécie de planta herbácea da família Zingiberaceae pertencente ao gênero Curcuma. Conhecida popularmente como Zedoária. Essa espécie é nativa do Sul e Sudeste da Ásia."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Temu putih",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temu_putih",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 28795628,
      "text": "Temu putih adalah salah satu spesies dari famili Zingiberaceae yang telah dikomersialkan penggunaan rhizomanya sebagai tanaman obat dan empon-empon. Temu putih disebut pula sebagai temu kuning. Produk alaminya banyak digunakan dalam industri parfum, pewarna untuk industri pangan, dan sebagai obat atau campuran obat. Khasiatnya bermacam-macam, tetapi biasanya terkait dengan pencernaan."
    }
  },
